{"kind":"request","text":"Operator-directed (2026-08-28; same sanction; priority 2 of 3). Two verified observability warts in tailapps/agent-guard. (a) folds/normalize.jsonata computes a single $reason string (session -\u003e tool -\u003e target precedence) and writes it to all three telemetry_coverage upserts, so a row's reason can explain a different capability's state: the live table shows every harness with capability tool-observation state=observed yet reason 'tool target absent, gated, or redacted' (the target-detail explanation). Make the reason per-capability so each row explains its own state. (b) With target detail redacted at default harness gates - the live norm: target-detail is unknown for all four observed harnesses - action_fingerprint degrades to harness|session|operation|tool|unknown, so repeated-action loop findings fire on any three consecutive same-tool calls regardless of arguments; live loop_findings is dominated by this (30 of 32 rows are repeated-action), and unlike policy_findings, loop rows carry no coverage qualifier marking that the fingerprint was degraded. Add a degradation marker so these findings are self-describing. Note the schema trade-off: a new column on the writable loop_findings table forces a reset activation (acknowledged data loss), while a marker inside the existing evidence JSON avoids any reset - builder judges the trade-off and documents whichever is chosen. Also document plainly that bounded-no-progress cannot fire until some harness emits progress fingerprints (progress-detail is unknown for all harnesses today). Verified against the live agent-guard projection and sources at local main 87a7c44b1816620e9947c33e2cad4d3c9e0ee9ca.","body":{"conditions":"Per-capability telemetry_coverage reasons; a degradation/coverage marker on repeated-action loop findings with the reset-vs-evidence trade-off addressed explicitly and documented; tests; full battery green; an effective checker review verdict at the exact implementation head.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}